A hook when tiny386 empties its TLB, for the fast path's own: a task switch reloads CR3 with the same value
as often as not (CWSDPMI, made for the 386, flushes the TLB that way), and that went unnoticed.

Beside tiny386's own tlb_gen (counted there for its fast/ path since 2d2e124): this firmware's fast path and
translator have their own TLBs and use the hook.

diff --git a/i386.c b/i386.c
index a3207c3..580a1c6 100644
--- a/i386.c
+++ b/i386.c
@@ -21,6 +21,11 @@
 #define T386_RAM_WRITE(cpu, addr, len) do {} while (0)
 #endif
 
+/* called when the TLB is emptied (MOV CR0/CR3, INVLPG, task switches): a translator's own TLB goes too */
+#ifndef T386_TLB_CLEARED
+#define T386_TLB_CLEARED() do {} while (0)
+#endif
+
 #define I386_OPT1
 #ifndef __wasm__
 #define I386_OPT2
@@ -555,6 +560,7 @@ static unsigned tlb_gen; /* counts TLB clears (fast/fast.h keeps a TLB of its ow
 
 static void tlb_clear(CPUI386 *cpu)
 {
+	T386_TLB_CLEARED();
 	tlb_gen++;
 	for (int i = 0; i < tlb_size; i++) {
 		cpu->tlb.tab[i].lpgno = -1;
